      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "源氏大将看了，自言自语地说：“她的字越写越好了。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "General Genji looked at it and murmured to himself, \"Her handwriting keeps getting better and better.\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "微笑地欣赏着。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "He admired it with a smile.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "他们常有书信往还，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "They often exchanged letters,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "所以她的笔迹很像源氏大将，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "so her handwriting greatly resembled General Genji's,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "近来越发秀丽，笔锋更添了妩媚。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and recently it had become even more elegant, with still more charm in the movement of the brush.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "源氏大将觉得这个人长育得一点缺陷也没有，",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "General Genji felt that as she had grown up, this person had developed without the slightest flaw,",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p01181",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "心中非常快慰。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "and he was deeply pleased in his heart.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
